  "purpose": "Determine whether a live KV tensor can be copied between CPU and GPU backing after context construction, whether the copy is correct, and whether the live decode graph actually consumes the relocated copy (true runtime relocation) or only a static-at-construction placement.",
  "literal_verdict": "LIVE_KV_COPY_WORKS_BUT_REBIND_STATIC",
  "verdict_summary": "Live CPU<->GPU KV copy is real, byte-verified, and precision-independent (Q8_0/Q5_1), reproduced at both tested model scales and at the real ctx=200000 pressure boundary, with <2% wall-clock stall for synchronous promotion. But llama_kv_cache::layers is a private field written once at construction and never again; the live decode graph keeps reading the ORIGINAL tensor, so every promotion/demotion this phase performs is a real, correct copy the decode graph never reads (poison-testing falsified live consumption in every trial). Source-level investigation (not inference) located the exact missing primitive: a relocate_layer-style method to reassign layers[il].k/.v after the copy -- not written this phase, per explicit instruction to stop and report.",
  "verdict_source": "results/phase12/promotion-prefetch/summary.json:decision_gate / decision_gate_meaning (literal source fields, not synthesized)",
  "productized": false,
  "product_pr": null,
  "product_commit": null,
  "productization_note": "No code from this branch (tools/membrane-kv-promotion-prefetch/) exists on product main. This phase's value is research-lineage only: it proved the copy primitive safe and precisely located the missing rebind primitive that Phase 12D went on to build. The product's static planner (PR #21) does not perform any live copy or promotion at all -- it decides placement once, before context construction, using only the Phase 12B mechanism.",
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
